# Typography System

Feel: Shopify POS / professional inventory software. Optimize for fast scanning, high
information density, minimal eye movement, all-day mobile use. No decorative type, no oversized
headings, no excess weights.

## Font

`Geist` primary, fallback `Inter, system-ui, sans-serif`. Enable tabular numerals
(`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` / Tailwind `tabular-nums`), antialiasing, optimized kerning.

## Weights — only three

- `400` Regular — body/secondary/captions
- `500` Medium — product names, labels, buttons
- `600` SemiBold — titles, primary numbers

Never use `700` Bold unless there is no other way to convey something critical.

## Scale (token → size / weight / line-height / usage)

| Tailwind utility | Size | Weight | Line height | Usage |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `text-page-title` | 20px | 600 | 28px | Page titles only (one per screen) |
| `text-section-title` | 17px | 600 | 24px | Section headers: Inventory, Categories, Reports |
| `text-row-title` | 15px | 500 | 20px | Primary list text — product names. First thing a user notices |
| `text-row-value` | 15px | 600 | 20px | Primary numbers — stock qty, prices. Always `tabular-nums` |
| `text-label` | 13px | 500 | 18px | Form field labels |
| `text-meta` | 12–13px | 400 | 18px | Secondary info: category, shelf, supplier (e.g. "Shelf A3 • Beverage • Updated today") |
| `text-input` (browser default `<input>`/`<Input>` size) | 16px | 400 | — | Form input text — 16px avoids iOS auto-zoom |
| `text-btn` | 14px | 500 | — | Button labels. Never bold |
| `text-caption` | 12px | 400 | 16px | "Last synced", "Created yesterday", helper text |

Do not invent new font sizes. Reuse these tokens everywhere. If a screen seems to need a new
size, it's almost always wrong — reach for weight, color, or spacing instead.

## Numbers

Every numeric value (stock qty, prices, counts) must:
- use `tabular-nums` so digits align vertically
- be right-aligned inside tables/rows
- use SemiBold (600) when it's the primary/important value (`text-row-value`)

## Color hierarchy (use color before size to establish hierarchy)

- Primary text — near-black (`text-foreground`)
- Secondary text — muted gray (`text-muted-foreground`)
- Disabled — light gray (`text-muted-foreground/50` or similar)
- Danger — red (`text-status-out` / `text-destructive`)
- Success — green (`text-status-available`)
- Warning — amber (`text-status-low`)

## Rules

1. Hierarchy comes from weight, spacing, and color — not from jumping font sizes.
2. Never introduce a font size outside the scale above without updating this rule first.
3. Keep line heights compact (see table) — avoid loose/airy spacing.
4. Layouts should fit ~10–14 inventory rows on a 6–7" phone screen without feeling cramped.
